wnloads available for every release. ripgrep is similar to other popular search tools like The Silver Searcher, ack and grep.","because it contains most of their features and is generally faster. (See the FAQ for more details on whether ripgrep can truly replace grep.)","recursive search and does automatic filtering. Namely, ripgrep won't search files ignored by your .gitignore/.ignore/.rgignore files, it won't search hidden files and it won't search binary files. Automatic filtering can be disabled with rg -uuu."],"features":["It can replace many use cases served by other search tools","Like other tools specialized to code search, ripgrep defaults to","ripgrep can search specific types of files.","ripgrep supports many features found in grep, such as showing the context","ripgrep has optional support for switching its regex engine to use PCRE2."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"945622d974f65e4e141ef9726c948c2640eebd222c5b101afb6445728283921e","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T06:01:31.192Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:25:20.799Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-08-04T13:59:44Z","demoHealth":{"url":"https://codapi.org/ripgrep/","attemptedAt":"2026-10-03T07:03:44.562Z","status":"working","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T07:03:44.562Z","lastWorkingAt":"2026-10-03T07:03:44.562Z","target":"https://codapi.org/ripgrep/","failureCount":0,"nextCheckAt":"2026-10-10T07:03:44.562Z"},"projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"ripgrep is a line-oriented search tool that recursively searches the current directory for a regex pattern. By default, ripgrep will respect gitignore rules and automatically skip hidden files/directories and binary files. (To disable all automatic filtering by default, use rg -uuu.) ripgrep has first class support on Windows, macOS and Linux, with binary downloads available for every release. ripgrep is similar to other popular search tools like The Silver Searcher, ack and grep.","sourceUrl":"https://